**(Textbook 7.2, HW7 Part A)** What is the running time of insertion sort if all N elements are equal? Justify with the code, and compare with presorted input.

```cpp
for( int p = 1; p < a.size( ); ++p )
{
    Comparable tmp = std::move( a[ p ] );
    int j;
    for( j = p; j > 0 && tmp < a[ j - 1 ]; --j )
        a[ j ] = std::move( a[ j - 1 ] );
    a[ j ] = std::move( tmp );
}
```
